WEBVTT

02:13.150 --> 02:15.209
This is taking longer than I expected.

02:19.356 --> 02:20.914
Let's get going, China Lilet!

02:31.969 --> 02:33.869
Oh, that was nice.

02:37.174 --> 02:38.642
Is that salt?

02:38.642 --> 02:40.132
I smell salt.

02:41.612 --> 02:43.512
We're coming up to the ocean.

02:44.215 --> 02:46.046
The eternal, ancient city of Revaiva.

02:46.917 --> 02:51.786
It originally began as a group who
formed with the ultimate goal

02:52.189 --> 02:54.525
of discovering the secret
to perpetual motion.

02:54.525 --> 02:57.517
Revaiva is the forbidden city they
eventually founded on the sea.

03:11.742 --> 03:13.209
It's the ocean!

03:21.385 --> 03:22.653
An island?

03:22.653 --> 03:27.352
The Eternal City of Revaiva
Part 2

03:28.092 --> 03:30.160
They felt, if they could develop
the art of perpetual motion,

03:30.160 --> 03:32.355
then they could apply that
to their own lives

03:32.863 --> 03:35.855
and discover the secret
to everlasting life.

03:36.400 --> 03:38.231
This is the greatest dream
in the history of mankind.

03:38.636 --> 03:42.072
They discovered how to live life free
of sickness and death, but...

03:43.540 --> 03:45.770
Is this the City of Revaiva?

03:46.610 --> 03:48.771
This isn't much of a city if you ask me.

03:54.618 --> 03:56.085
There's no sign of life anywhere.

03:56.453 --> 03:57.955
I always thought this town would be
bustling with joyous people

03:57.955 --> 03:59.786
who had been freed from
worrying about death.

04:00.324 --> 04:02.660
Man, and I was planning
on being greeted

04:02.660 --> 04:04.992
by all the beautiful women
living for eternity!

04:06.030 --> 04:07.497
Oh, Kir, you're so cool!

04:09.400 --> 04:11.197
I guess there will be
no welcome wagon,

04:11.635 --> 04:13.933
or kisses from beautiful girls
for that matter.

04:22.613 --> 04:25.349
Looks like this became a city of death

04:25.349 --> 04:26.816
rather than a city of eternal life.

04:27.451 --> 04:30.750
The secret of their discovery must
never be taken from the island.

04:31.422 --> 04:34.191
It is said that those who try
to leave this eternal island

04:34.191 --> 04:36.318
with the secret will lose their lives.

04:36.727 --> 04:39.093
It is a strict custom that they
take very seriously here.

04:44.068 --> 04:46.127
Is there really just no one here?

04:46.537 --> 04:49.973
Seems like Hell would be
more fun than this place.

04:52.810 --> 04:54.778
Hey, there's someone over there!

04:58.315 --> 04:59.782
Isn't that a statue?

05:00.684 --> 05:04.848
Who would make such an ugly thing?
Maybe someone got Lonely?

05:05.222 --> 05:09.056
If you seek to be happy for two hours,
you should drink some wine.

05:09.593 --> 05:13.552
If you seek to be happy for three
hours, you should get married.

05:16.066 --> 05:19.502
If you seek to be happy for eternity,

05:20.537 --> 05:23.005
learn how to fish!

05:29.446 --> 05:32.711
You passed the test, my little minstrel.

05:34.451 --> 05:37.888
I have been waiting for you
for quite a while now.

05:37.888 --> 05:41.289
How many thousands of years
has it been?

05:42.292 --> 05:44.226
I got a bite! It's a big one!

05:47.765 --> 05:50.825
You're not getting away this time,
Mr. Leviathan!

06:06.850 --> 06:10.752
Your old, decaying body can't
take much more of this.

06:11.255 --> 06:12.722
It's useless to put up a fight.

06:13.657 --> 06:16.956
That's a fresh piece of sushi fish!
He'll definitely be worth frying!

06:22.900 --> 06:24.333
Kir!

06:26.403 --> 06:27.870
Kir Royale!

06:36.246 --> 06:37.981
Vermouth!?

06:37.981 --> 06:40.951
Hey, Jing! Vermouth isn't breathing!

06:40.951 --> 06:42.418
What?!

06:42.853 --> 06:45.321
Don't you boys worry your
pretty little heads.

06:45.823 --> 06:48.348
It doesn't look good.
I'll check her out.

06:51.028 --> 06:54.327
Her heart has stopped!
What should we do?!

06:54.932 --> 06:57.167
I've been the undying king here
for a long time.

06:57.167 --> 06:59.897
Don't worry, I'm an expert
on keeping things alive.

07:02.439 --> 07:04.270
The eternal life that was
discovered in that city

07:04.675 --> 07:07.576
has been found nowhere
else in the world.

07:08.045 --> 07:10.639
Because everyone who escapes
is killed, the city's secret

07:11.114 --> 07:13.844
and location have never been
revealed to the outside world.

07:14.218 --> 07:16.220
There seems to be no way to
discover this secret city,

07:16.220 --> 07:17.847
even for those of us who search
for it our entire lives.

07:19.323 --> 07:22.053
Amazing! Simply amazing!

07:22.559 --> 07:25.892
We are about to go where no outsiders
have gone before us.

07:26.163 --> 07:28.232
We will soon know the
secrets of eternal life

07:28.232 --> 07:29.699
and the Water of Unending Life!

07:30.767 --> 07:33.670
I will finally cross over
into eternal life,

07:33.670 --> 07:36.798
and sit on the throne above
all living things forever!

07:46.049 --> 07:49.753
I've been alive so long, I easily forget
names of things I learned long ago.

07:49.753 --> 07:52.449
I even forget what everyday
words mean.

07:52.890 --> 07:57.054
There is simply no room left in my
brain for any new information.

07:57.528 --> 08:00.395
Isn't that normal for someone
as old as you are?

08:01.732 --> 08:03.600
Maybe you're right.

08:03.600 --> 08:06.831
That's why I use these name tags to
remember what things are called.

08:08.672 --> 08:10.902
When you're my age, you'll wish
you had them too.

08:15.579 --> 08:20.417
Especially if you become the next
undying king, Mr. Minstrel.

08:20.417 --> 08:23.511
Hey mister, what have you been
doing here all this time?

08:24.021 --> 08:27.057
I have been researching
perpetual motion.

08:27.057 --> 08:28.820
How to make it, and what it
exactly means.

08:31.328 --> 08:34.865
Hey, I can't tell you how many times
I have failed.

08:34.865 --> 08:37.935
One idea I had was that one could
live twice as long as normal

08:37.935 --> 08:40.837
if they always kept one eye closed,
alternating between the two.

08:40.837 --> 08:43.397
I tested this theory on a cow, but only
her eyes lived twice as long.

08:43.807 --> 08:45.475
This little wind-up car here
was designed

08:45.475 --> 08:47.344
around the idea of the never-ending,
one-sided Moebius strip,

08:47.344 --> 08:49.676
but it only moves in small,
sudden bursts.

08:50.447 --> 08:53.348
I became incredibly discouraged
after I designed this guy.

08:53.850 --> 08:55.018
A lion?

08:55.018 --> 08:57.953
No, not just a lion. He's the king
of all beasts!

08:58.388 --> 09:00.090
I installed a perpetual motion
machine in his mane,

09:00.090 --> 09:01.592
but it didn't make him
live any longer.

09:01.592 --> 09:03.116
Now he's a lyin' dead lion.

09:03.760 --> 09:05.227
Lyin' dead lion?

09:06.063 --> 09:07.464
To tell you the truth,

09:07.464 --> 09:09.022
very few of my experiments were
as successful as this guy.

09:09.900 --> 09:12.767
Oh, this one! He was the one
who gave us the ride.

09:19.376 --> 09:22.345
This is my assistant, Villar.

09:26.450 --> 09:28.385
What's this?!

09:28.385 --> 09:30.717
Is this the famous eternal city
of Revaiva?!

09:31.288 --> 09:32.990
What the hell has happened here?!

09:32.990 --> 09:35.559
What happened to all the people who
are supposed to have eternal life?!

09:35.559 --> 09:38.562
Where have they all gone?

09:38.562 --> 09:42.132
But wait, they couldn't have all left.

09:42.132 --> 09:43.500
I'm sure they're hiding out,

09:43.500 --> 09:44.901
protecting the Water of Unending Life.

09:44.901 --> 09:46.835
They've got to be here somewhere.

09:47.404 --> 09:48.871
Let's go, China Lilet!

09:49.406 --> 09:51.908
But before we do,

09:51.908 --> 09:53.432
why don't we give you that little
upgrade we were talking about?

10:07.357 --> 10:10.326
Hey, by the way, mister,
how is Vermouth doing?

10:11.461 --> 10:16.066
Check it out, all he's doing
is rubbing her body.

10:16.066 --> 10:17.829
Hey, let me help you with that!

10:18.602 --> 10:21.038
I promise you, she'll be alright.

10:21.038 --> 10:23.907
Nothing too bad can really happen
to Vermouth here.

10:23.907 --> 10:25.475
Hey, can I help with that?!

10:25.475 --> 10:27.636
After all, I was the one
who made her.

10:30.981 --> 10:33.950
She utilizes my best perpetual
motion machine to date,

10:33.950 --> 10:35.645
the Odoradic engine.

10:39.122 --> 10:41.090
That should do the trick.

10:49.132 --> 10:52.069
King Cointreau! Oh, no!

10:52.069 --> 10:55.205
We already know about everything!

10:55.205 --> 10:57.841
We figured out your little
set up a while back!

10:57.841 --> 10:59.776
Are you going to tell on me?

10:59.776 --> 11:01.712
What are we going to say?

11:01.712 --> 11:03.413
Hey c'mon, settle down.

11:03.413 --> 11:05.248
I would never have been able to find
this legendary minstrel

11:05.248 --> 11:08.445
if it were not for the work
of Vermouth here.

11:08.685 --> 11:11.755
You've been calling me that
ever since I got here.

11:11.755 --> 11:13.222
What does it mean?

11:15.092 --> 11:16.457
Well, that...

11:25.102 --> 11:27.263
Let's go, China Lilet!

11:30.107 --> 11:32.576
The blue bird with a crown
of flowers atop his head

11:32.576 --> 11:34.908
closes his beautiful wings
of freedom and lands,

11:35.312 --> 11:37.280
positioning himself lightly on
the shoulders of the minstrel,

11:38.014 --> 11:41.882
who has one leg lifted up to his chest,

11:42.319 --> 11:44.287
and quietly played his harp.

11:47.090 --> 11:50.060
Those words are sung about
the legendary minstrel,

11:50.060 --> 11:52.290
who, it is said, will become
our next undying king.

11:53.096 --> 11:55.758
That is exactly how she saw you land

11:56.233 --> 11:57.768
back in the field right outside
of the capital of Corpus.

11:57.768 --> 12:01.465
From that moment, she was sure
that she had found you.

12:12.516 --> 12:16.509
When I first heard about you
I had my doubts, but now...

12:16.820 --> 12:19.389
I told you it was him, didn't I?

12:19.389 --> 12:24.326
And Jing totally passed all the tests
and made it all the way here.

12:24.694 --> 12:27.831
Hey, I hate to throw a wrench
in this perfect story,

12:27.831 --> 12:31.130
but I'm a black bird, not blue.
And Jing doesn't even own a harp!

12:31.434 --> 12:33.959
Sometimes real life is allowed
to vary slightly from legend.

12:36.006 --> 12:40.705
He also beat everyone from the
skeleton captain to Mr. Leviathan.

12:41.444 --> 12:45.248
I'm positive that you are to be
the next undying king, Jing.

12:45.248 --> 12:47.384
I am sure that once you take over
my position you'll be able to find

12:47.384 --> 12:49.716
the answers to all of the questions
that I was never able to answer.

12:57.227 --> 12:59.388
You've definitely got a long life
ahead of you.

12:59.930 --> 13:03.229
You have plenty of time to tell him
all about it. Don't stress out.

13:05.769 --> 13:09.933
Here's some soup.

13:10.307 --> 13:11.774
Oh, thank you!

13:14.578 --> 13:17.411
What is this? It tastes just
like normal water!

13:18.348 --> 13:20.550
Yea, but no matter how hungry
you get, you'll never die.

13:20.550 --> 13:23.420
You don't have to eat anything
if you don't want to.

13:23.420 --> 13:25.581
Sorry, this is just one way to hold on
to the old way of life.

13:25.989 --> 13:29.789
Now I just like to call it eternity soup.

13:30.293 --> 13:32.896
Eternity soup?! But it has no
special taste or anything!

13:32.896 --> 13:34.464
It's just normal water!

13:34.464 --> 13:37.133
Yes, but during all of these
isolated years,

13:37.133 --> 13:42.072
it helped him remember
that he is alive. I get it.

13:42.072 --> 13:44.632
What? What do you mean, Jing?

13:45.175 --> 13:47.477
It's just that I have so much free time.

13:47.477 --> 13:49.446
Speaking of fun,

13:49.446 --> 13:52.279
sometimes as I go to bed I have him
read me this Ohanashi.

13:52.682 --> 13:55.452
Ohanashi? Is that a book?
A collection of old poems?

13:55.452 --> 13:57.079
Are you just talking crazy?

13:57.888 --> 14:00.223
Maybe I am crazy.

14:00.223 --> 14:01.591
This is the Water of Unending Life.

14:01.591 --> 14:03.093
It now belongs to the two of you.

14:03.093 --> 14:06.927
The Water of Unending Life! Is that
what gives you everlasting life?

14:07.597 --> 14:09.266
What happens if we drink it?

14:09.266 --> 14:11.496
Will we be able to live forever?

14:12.602 --> 14:14.571
But didn't everyone in
the town drink this?

14:14.571 --> 14:17.107
Why are you the only one left
living out your eternal life here?

14:17.107 --> 14:18.574
What happened?

14:18.808 --> 14:22.300
They all chose to abandon their
eternity and leave this place.

14:22.612 --> 14:24.848
Hold on, let me get this straight.

14:24.848 --> 14:26.315
They all had eternal life, but just
decided to throw it all away?!

14:26.816 --> 14:28.579
It's true.

14:46.670 --> 14:49.070
Nobody could find it.

14:49.773 --> 14:52.309
King Cointreau is still looking
for the same thing to this day,

14:52.309 --> 14:53.776
the meaning of everlasting life.

14:54.577 --> 14:56.479
But why? What happened?

14:56.479 --> 14:59.282
Wasn't this whole place a fantastic
eternal paradise?

14:59.282 --> 15:01.785
You guys must be leaving
something out!

15:01.785 --> 15:04.888
What does all this eternal, undying
life business even mean?!

15:04.888 --> 15:07.755
I'm beginning to think this legendary
paradise is all a hoax!

15:08.158 --> 15:10.422
Sometimes real life is allowed
to vary slightly from legend.

15:11.094 --> 15:12.561
Right?

15:15.765 --> 15:18.825
And now I can finally join the
rest of them in that world.

15:22.439 --> 15:27.077
So, King Cointreau, you're
looking forward to

15:27.077 --> 15:29.079
going back to a world that
isn't free from death?

15:29.079 --> 15:31.514
Hey c'mon, take it from
me, it's not that great.

15:31.514 --> 15:33.607
Don't tell me you want
to give this all up!

15:34.184 --> 15:36.486
I can tell you still got thousands
of years left in you, old man.

15:36.486 --> 15:39.421
You don't want to do this.

15:39.990 --> 15:42.492
No, no, trust me, I'm quite sure.

15:42.492 --> 15:43.959
You can't be serious.

15:55.605 --> 15:58.130
Him again! You notice anything
different about him?

15:58.508 --> 16:00.110
I thought he was
expressionless before,

16:00.110 --> 16:01.839
but now I can't even see
the slightest sign of life.

16:03.646 --> 16:06.850
Sorry, I've never really been a big fan
of peaceful negotiations.

16:06.850 --> 16:08.485
I have come to claim what
is rightfully mine.

16:08.485 --> 16:11.888
I made it here, so I deserve to drink
and receive eternal life!

16:11.888 --> 16:13.590
You really don't understand, do you?

16:13.590 --> 16:17.093
Even your refined ways can't save you
from the perils of this drink!

16:17.093 --> 16:18.822
Go, China Lilet!

16:28.138 --> 16:32.302
That's right, China Lilet! Show them
the power of your new upgrade!

16:36.513 --> 16:40.347
Jing! Just aim for that triangle
above his head!

16:42.585 --> 16:44.212
All right, let's go Kir!

16:57.734 --> 16:59.201
Kir Royale!

17:04.441 --> 17:05.241
It didn't work!

17:05.241 --> 17:06.576
No way!

17:06.576 --> 17:09.479
Not much longer now,
soon it will be mine!

17:09.479 --> 17:10.847
I will be the richest man alive!

17:10.847 --> 17:12.872
Basking in the pleasure of eternal life!

17:15.552 --> 17:17.320
Let me borrow this.

17:17.320 --> 17:18.787
Kir, let's go!

17:23.359 --> 17:24.826
Kir Royale!

17:40.777 --> 17:43.546
I'm sorry. It got a little messed up.

17:43.546 --> 17:45.537
Jing, what's going to happen to them?

17:46.049 --> 17:48.885
When the big one moves, it tickles
the little one and makes him laugh.

17:48.885 --> 17:51.121
That in turn makes him
move the controller,

17:51.121 --> 17:53.112
which causes the big one
to move again.

17:56.259 --> 17:57.894
They're a living perpetual
motion machine.

17:57.894 --> 17:59.796
The perpetual Laughter of Hell.

17:59.796 --> 18:01.598
They'll be going on like that forever?

18:01.598 --> 18:02.732
I almost feel sorry for them.

18:02.732 --> 18:06.369
But wouldn't it be great to be able
to laugh for the rest of eternity?

18:06.369 --> 18:07.836
You really think so?

18:08.204 --> 18:11.037
What do you think, mister, of my own
perpetual motion machine?

18:15.145 --> 18:16.880
Mister?

18:16.880 --> 18:18.347
King Cointreau?

18:22.051 --> 18:23.814
Is he really gone?

18:24.287 --> 18:26.687
King Cointreau...

18:32.862 --> 18:34.352
Thank you...

18:35.031 --> 18:38.967
Drinking and drinking the wine,
without rest or reward.

18:39.536 --> 18:42.061
He'd been living his life
in that daze for so long.

18:48.478 --> 18:51.072
One king dies, and a new one is born.

19:00.356 --> 19:02.381
It is the way of life.

19:08.364 --> 19:12.664
I guess life and death are like
two sides of the same coin.

19:14.704 --> 19:16.228
What are you trying to say Jing?

19:16.873 --> 19:18.308
On the front side of
this coin is Corpus,

19:18.308 --> 19:20.076
the town where journeys begin.

19:20.076 --> 19:21.578
And on the back is Revaiva,

19:21.578 --> 19:23.045
the town where journeys end.

19:31.421 --> 19:33.981
Stretching from the lake...

19:34.390 --> 19:38.486
To the farm...

19:38.928 --> 19:43.666
Hey, Villar, your master is dead now,
don't you get it?

19:43.666 --> 19:47.534
Roger, everywhere he...

19:48.037 --> 19:50.440
Hey, what's wrong? Is he broken?

19:50.440 --> 19:52.601
He's fine Kir, just let him continue.

19:52.842 --> 19:55.777
Sitting upon a stone...

19:56.179 --> 20:00.047
Listening to the stars...

20:00.984 --> 20:03.253
Villar is reading him the Ohanashi

20:03.253 --> 20:05.154
so that King Cointreau won't
get bored in his dreams.

20:05.154 --> 20:07.824
He will continue to talk like this until
King Cointreau wakes up.

20:07.824 --> 20:09.519
So, basically for eternity.

20:10.460 --> 20:15.098
The deep land and...

20:15.098 --> 20:21.799
The blue sea rustle...

20:36.352 --> 20:37.819
Hey, Jing!

20:39.522 --> 20:42.616
Hey, if you're going to drink that,
be sure and save some for me!

21:01.277 --> 21:04.940
Kir, I forgot about one of the
most important things in life.

21:06.683 --> 21:11.347
If I were to drink this, I'd never be
able to see my mom again.

21:12.288 --> 21:14.257
Jing!

21:14.257 --> 21:15.724
Jing, you...

21:23.599 --> 21:27.729
All I'm saying is that shining
brightly for a split second

21:28.104 --> 21:30.265
is better than living a dull,
gray life in eternity.
